{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Separate yourselves from the midst of this assembly.</b> This is the assembly of Korah, for Moses and Aaron were together with them at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting. Moses thought that 'this assembly' referred to all Israel, and therefore he answered Him, 'Shall one man sin and will You be wrathful against the whole assembly?' And the Holy One, blessed be He, immediately clarified for him that the assembly spoken of is the assembly of Korah, as it says, 'Get you up from about the tabernacle of Korah.' If so, 'get you up' (העלו) is the interpretation of 'separate yourselves' (הבדלו). And as for why He needed to say 'Separate yourselves' — seeing that the Holy One, blessed be He, has it in His power to put to death and to bring to life, and no separation is necessary before Him, for He can slay the many and deliver the individual among them, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: two or three were wrapped in a single cloak — the two would die and the one in the middle would be saved, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 91:7): ״יפול מצדך אלף ורבבה מימינך אליך לא יגש״ — 'A thousand shall fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand; it shall not come near you' — if so, what need was there to say 'Separate yourselves'? Rather, it was so that the foul air of the plague would not cleave to them, in the manner stated regarding the wife of Lot (Genesis 19:26): ״ותבט אשתו מאחריו ותהי נציב מלח״ — 'And his wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt.' Or for the reason our Rabbis of blessed memory stated: when the attribute of justice is stretched out, it does not distinguish between righteous and wicked. Or it is possible to say that He spoke thus for the honor of the righteous, that the Holy One, blessed be He, would not send His hand against them while the righteous were among them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:07.172169177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}